  "findings": [
    "All three positive natural requests and the worksite control received the same generic clarification. No immediate pin or selectable alternative appeared. Every natural reply arrived by 3.947 seconds. The negative was withheld procedurally, with no explanation of the construction barrier.",
    "The marked bay beside the pink wall and the empty parking row ahead of the red SUV at night both accepted and saved the passenger’s exact original-pixel tap. The open gravel entrance beside a hedge was classified as sidewalk and withheld. Each dedicated traffic-lane tap and the explicit coned-worksite mark withheld. The stripe in the night parking row offered no adjacent point.",
    "The pink-wall photograph already had three local two-view OPEN points in its target, out of twelve proposed points. The three corresponding point captions omitted the wall and its colour. The full-image bands mention a mosque and the Environmental and Protected Areas Authority. The guided language parser did not recognize the request.",
    "The gravel entrance had zero measured candidates and a sidewalk label at the reference tap. The night photograph had one two-view OPEN point with a correctly described red SUV and white sedan, but the point lay outside the frozen empty-row region. The original reference tap had a parking label and the original stripe had a paint label."
